# Single-store boundary

AAURIKAA is a **single-business** jewellery store, not a marketplace.

## Seller compatibility

- Backend may still require a `Seller` document for ownership, GST origin, Shiprocket, returns spine, etc.
- Treat Seller as an **internal** compatibility entity (foundation already pins Admin writes to the internal Seller).
- Do not make Admin or customers choose a seller.

## Do not expose (unless explicitly requested)

- Seller marketplace browsing, public seller storefronts, seller onboarding
- Seller selection / picker in Admin workflows
- Commissions, payouts, seller ledgers, marketplace finance UI
- “Become a seller” / seller FAQ / seller portal surfaces in AAURIKAA UX

## Allowed

- Keeping seller routes/models in the codebase while disabled or unused by AAURIKAA UI
- Admin operating as the store operator (not as multi-vendor marketplace admin)

When adding navigation, APIs, or copy: default to **hide marketplace concepts**.
